lessons.body:
Health, Liveness, Readiness, and Graceful
Shutdown

A process can be alive but not ready to serve real traffic. TaskFlow separates those concepts so
deployment infrastructure can make the right decision.

critical dependencies usable;
/health/live                             process can respond; /health/ready       deploy/router sends traffic only
when ready
→                                        →

Figure 4. Health semantics

@Get('live')
live() {
return { status: 'ok' };
}

@Get('ready')
@HealthCheck()
ready() {
return this.health.check([
() => this.prismaHealth.pingCheck('database', this.prisma),
]);
}

NestJS Terminus provides readiness/liveness health-check support and includes a
PrismaHealthIndicator. Enable shutdown hooks so the application can transition cleanly during
termination.

• Liveness should be cheap and should not fail merely because an external dependency has a
transient issue.

• Readiness may check PostgreSQL and other truly required dependencies.

• Do not put slow external calls to every third-party API into every probe.

• Health responses must not expose credentials, connection strings, internal topology, or stack traces.

Sentry Error Monitoring for NestJS and
Next.js

Sentry complements the public error envelope from Phase 13. Clients still receive safe error
responses; Sentry receives actionable exception context, release/environment data, and performance
evidence according to privacy policy.
// apps/api/src/instrument.ts - import before other app modules
import * as Sentry from '@sentry/nestjs';

Sentry.init({
dsn: process.env.SENTRY_DSN,
environment: process.env.NODE_ENV,
tracesSampleRate: 0.1,
});

The current Sentry NestJS SDK requires the instrumentation import to happen before other application
modules so automatic instrumentation can initialize correctly. The Next.js SDK can similarly capture
unhandled errors and performance data.

Attach useful, safe context
Sentry.setTag('request_id', requestId);
Sentry.setTag('workspace_id', workspaceId);
Sentry.setUser({ id: userId }); // only if your privacy policy permits

Sentry.captureException(error);

Production caution: Never send access tokens, refresh tokens, cookies, uploaded document contents,
passwords, or secrets to error monitoring. Review PII policy, scrubbing, and retention before
production.

